Matrix 3 and 5 kVA UPS from American Power Conversion

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Matrix series of uninterruptible power systems features leadership
   price/performance, provides 100 percent uptime at 60 percent lower
   operating cost

o  Systems include:
   - Modular design with user friendly diagnostics -- modules hot swappable
     by untrained personnel
   - Plug-and-play battery pack and output receptacle extensions
   - 3 year onsite warranty for units sold in U.S.
   - Continuous no-break regulation; filtering over wide input voltage range
     in both normal and utility failure modes, with full isolation in bypass
   - $25,000 "absolute" warranty coverage for any damage to protected
     systems

o  PowerChute plus software provides realtime monitoring and automatic,
   orderly CPU shutdown during prolonged power outage

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The Matrix series from American Power Conversion is a best-in-class
line-interactive UPS. It provides online performance without sacrificing
efficiency and its line interactive design provides superior power
conditioning. The Matrix series also provides maximum brown-out protection
through "Fine Line" voltage regulation, handling low voltage conditions of
up to 25 percent below nominal. Models are available in both 3 kVA and 5 kVA
North American and worldwide versions, with 3 kVA/2250 W and 5 kVA/3750 W
single-phase output ratings.

The Matrix series is specifically designed to support client/server and
workgroup computing environments with a need for distributed UPS solutions.
In addition, APC's PowerChute Plus software and network SNMP adapters
provide monitoring, safe unattended shutdown, and network power management
solutions for most operating systems, including the DEC OSF/1 and Windows NT
operating systems.

With the Matrix series Digital is expanding its suite of APC products,
providing a wider range of low cost, reliable power protection solutions.
Product ratings now range from 250 VA to 5 kVA.

Modular Design

A Matrix UPS is made up of three modules and is easy to install. It is the
only UPS in its class that lets the user swap out modules quickly and safely
without disconnecting the critical load. Its electronic module has an MTBF
of about 12 years. It sits on an isolation module with an MTBF of about 99
years. The third module is an external, stackable, plug-and-play SmartCell
battery pack with a six year average life.

The electronic module furnishes conditioned power via the battery should the
utility fail or go outside of acceptable limits. It contains the main
processor voltage regulator, inverter/battery charger electronics, and a
programmable front panel display. The specially designed battery charger
allows substantially improved recharge times approaching half the industry
norm.

The isolation unit in conjunction with the Fine Line regulator in the
electronics module provides all power conditioning to the load in normal
operation. It contains a bypass circuit, an input/output power module, and
an isolation transformer. Full isolation in both normal and bypass mode
provides an improved barrier for EMI, while the regenerated neutral
eliminates unwanted harmonics in the building distribution system. Unlike
competing products, this UPS does not require that the input voltage match
the output voltage in bypass.

Each battery pack contains a microprocessor that monitors the battery status
and reports to the electronics module through a communications interface.
Typical battery times for 3 kVA and 5 kVA systems are seven to eight minutes
at full load. Users can extend battery time easily by plugging in additional
battery cabinets as needed (see the Matrix Model Run and Recharge Times
section below).

All three modules meet UL, CSA, and TUV requirements for safety and FCC and
CDC requirements for EMC verification.

Monitoring Features

The programmable, 2 x 16 character LCD display is available in four
languages; it includes load power, voltage, and intelligent run time meters,
adjustable sensitivity, and both automatic and requested self-tests. The UPS
also includes an intelligent, user-switchable bypass that works with the
isolation module to ensure auomatic, no-break transfer in the event of
inverter failure. The UPS also has an external Emergency Power Off (EPO)
interface.

Models

The North American UPS is designed to support a nominal single-phase input
voltage of 208 V at 60 Hz and an output voltage of 120/240 V (L14-30R) and
208 V (L6-30R). With special ordering and configuration provisions, it can
also handle 240 V input for users limited to 240 V split-phase power.

This model comes standard with a six foot input cord and L6-30P plug and
with an output power distribution module that houses three 5-15R2
receptacles: two L6-30R types and one L14-30R type. If desired it can also
be optionally hardwired on the input at the user's site. Optional
cord/plug-connected power distribution modules can be added to the standard
output receptacle configuration for additional outlets and can be easily
swapped out as equipment needs change. In addition, a hardwired kit allows
the output to be optionally hardwired to a remote distribution panel.

The worldwide UPS is designed to support a nominal single-phase input
voltage of 220, 230, or 240 V (user selectable) at 50 or 60 Hz and is user
programmable to allow a 220, 225, 230, or 240 V output. Frequency is
automatically sensed and voltage selections are via the front panel. The
unit is hardwired on the input and includes four IEC 320 10A and four IEC
320 16A output receptacles. With special ordering and configuration
provisions, this model can also handle 208 V input and 120 V loads on the
output for special situations.

All models have an acceptable input voltage range of -25 percent to +15
percent within the selected nominal setting and a +/- 5 percent output
voltage regulation with <5 percent output voltage THD on the battery. The
5 kVA model is derated to 4.7 kVA when configured for 208 V on the output.

Options

Among the options available are Power Doctor diagnostic software for MS-DOS,
a Call-UPS telephone-actuated on/off control for unattended remote computer
operations, a Measure-UPS environmental monitoring interface, Power Manager
power cable management and surge protection, and SNMP adapters for full
network management and control.

BENEFITS

o  Complete blackout and brownout protection.
o  Network grade conditioning (Novell approved).
o  Lightning and surge protection.
o  Hot swap of the electronic and battery modules without powering down the
   UPS.
o  Audible alarms.
o  A two-year hot swap vendor-return warranty with an optional three-year
   onsite offering.
o  A line-interactive design providing superior conditioning even in
   maintenance bypass.
o  A battery replacement warning.
o  An intelligent Fine Line voltage regulation unit that learns site
   characteristics to minimize battery usage.
o  Site and unit diagnostics, with load status indicated.
o  Programmable remote test provisions.
o  Network EIA 232 interface port with SNMP provisions.
o  APC's "ABSOLUTE Protection" guarantee. Under this guarantee, APC will
   repair or replace any equipment (with a value of up to $25,000) damaged
   by a surge while the equipment is protected by a properly installed
   Matrix UPS. Terms and conditions of the program are shipped with the
   product.

MATRIX MODEL RUN AND RECHARGE TIMES

In the following tabulation, battery run and recharge times are compared for
the 3 kVA and 5 kVA Matrix models. The times are shown in hours and are
based on a typical computer load at 0.65 pf. The standard models include one
3 kVA battery pack and two 5 kVA battery packs. The recharge is to 90
percent capacity after discharge into a 50 percent rated load. Two
SmartCells provide 500 W; more than two SmartCells provide 1000 W.

