 news0601.txt;- Digital POLYCENTER Manager on NetView - Info Sheet

 PRODUCT NAME:  POLYCENTER Manager on NetView for DEC OSF/1 AXP

 DESCRIPTION

 The POLYCENTER Manager on NetView (POLYCENTER NetView) provides a
 comprehensive network management solution for heterogeneous multi-
 vendor network devices and open client/server networked environments.
 It includes user-oriented SNMP applications for fault, configuration,
 and performance management; and standard application programming inter-
 faces (APIs) that allow software developers to seamlessly integrate
 their multiprotocol applications.

 POLYCENTER Manager on NetView incorporates the guidelines and
 definitions programmers need to create SNMP or CMIP applications that
 can work together to provide end-to-end management of enterprise
 information systems.

 Features/Benefits:

 Superior Graphical User Interface:

 o  View network at a single glance to rapidly recognize and resolve
    network problems

 o  "Out of the box" functionality provides immediate results

 o  Advanced human factors engineering provides simple, easy-to-
    understand display with excellent window management to minimize
    screen clutter

    -  Topology View - displays and manages network maps
    -  Control Desk - displays and manages network events and other
       applications
    -  Tool Palette - provides fast and easy access to most frequently
       used tools
    -  Navigation Tree - keeps users organized as they traverse the
       network

 o  Network views may be customized based on any criteria: geography,
    physical or logical layout, device-type, etc.

 o  Easily add customized backgrounds and icons

 o  Context-sensitive pop up menus provide user with set of commands
    applicable to selected object

 o  Monitor information for real-time trouble diagnosis, comparison
    against thresholds, and historical report generation

 o  Show real-time and historical graphs of network statistics

 Application Programming Interfaces (APIs)

 Open and industry standard interfaces permit seamless integration of
 other management applications:

 o  End-User Interface API - enables applications to be integrated as
    part of the graphical display

 o  SNMP API - enables applications to access MIB information

 o  Event Filtering API - provides filter definitions and thresholding
    of event information sent to events display, POLYCENTER Manager on
    NetView applications, or other registered applications

 o  XMP (X/Open Management Protocol) API - provides SNMP and CMIP over
    TCP/IP (CMOT) support based on OSF DME technology and provides an
    object oriented API to accommodate customer needs

 Dynamic Network Discovery

 o  Automatically discovers, maps, and monitors TCP/IP network resources

 o  Changes are also discovered, and automatically reflected on the
    appropriate submaps. Newly discovered objects may be automatically
    placed on the appropriate submap, or optionally stored in a holding
    area for later manual placement.

 o  Automatic topology mapping includes support for ring, bus, tree and
    star layouts to portray complex customer environments

 Real-time Administrative Change Capability

 o  Operational parameters may be changed in real-time without
    disrupting ongoing data collection

 Management Information Base (MIB) Processing

 o  Includes support for MIB-2 objects and many pre-loaded vendor
    extensions

 o  MIB Loader allows any enterprise-specific MIB extension to be added

 o  MIB Data Collector allows collection of real-time or historical MIB
    information and compares data to user defined thresholds to generate
    events

 o  MIB Browser allows for browsing, retrieving, or setting MIB values

 o  MIB Application Builder allows development of applications without
    any programming, which includes retrieval of data, graphic or
    tabular display, or storing data as a file

 Open Topology Manager

 o  Expands the scope of POLYCENTER Manager on NetView beyond SNMP by
    allowing the integration and correlation of multiple protocol
    topologies within topology maps and event displays. Protocols such
    as DECnet can be integrated via the Topology Manager.

 Filtering Capabilities

 o  Helps to weed out extraneous information and provide greater control

 o  Filtering criteria can be applied to event information that is
    displayed on the screen, or sent to applications

 o  Automates actions to be taken as a result of standard and
    enterprise-specific SNMP traps

 POLYCENTER Manager on NetView provides network management functionality
 in three critical areas:

 o  Fault Management
 o  Configuration Management
 o  Performance Management

 These management applications are included as part of the product and
 may be enhanced by the numerous applications provided by third party
 vendors.

 Strengths:

 o  Jointly developed and will be jointly enhanced by both Digital and
    IBM[R]

 o  Synchronized product releases and enhancements by Digital and IBM

 o  Joint Marketing, and NetView Association (applications) with IBM

 o  Established and Proven Technology - based on Hewlett-Packard[R]'s
    OpenView, enhanced by IBM

 o  Superior SNMP Manager, including these enhancements over HP[R]'s
    OpenView:

    -  Top rated Graphical User Interface
    -  Window Management/Navigation Tree
    -  Tool Palette, Control Desk, MIB Browser and Application Builder
    -  Storage and display of topology from multiple protocols
    -  Robust Event Handling
    -  Enhanced Filtering and Thresholding capabilities
    -  Resulting in High End-User Productivity

 o  Common Application APIs

 o  Integration point for System and Network management applications

 o  Superior price/performance of Alpha AXP

 o  Third party applications available today, and many more to be
    announced very soon

 o  SNA/CORBA support available soon

 o  DECnet support available (see Optional Software section below)

 POLYCENTER Manager on NetView is supported by the joint Digital and IBM
 NetView Association, a joint ISV association which includes over 100
 software vendors committed to developing and/or porting third party
 applications for POLYCENTER Manager on NetView.

 POLYCENTER Migration software packages will be available in Q4 FY94 to
 facilitate the transition from POLYCENTER Network Manager 200/400 and
 POLYCENTER SNMP Manager 100/300 to the POLYCENTER Manager on NetView
 for DEC OSF/1 AXP and POLYCENTER DECnet Manager on NetView for DEC
 OSF/1 AXP.

 Digital advantages:

 o  NetView offered on high performance Alpha AXP processors

 o  Superior Price/Performance

 o  Superior Graphical User Interface, intuitive and easy to use

 o  Common APIs which are open and extensible

 CONFORMANCE TO STANDARDS

 POLYCENTER Manager on NetView conforms to the Internet Engineering Task
 Force (IETF) defined framework for network management. It conforms
 specifically to the following IETF RFCs:

 o  RFC1157
 o  RFC1155
 o  RFC1213

 POLYCENTER Manager on NetView is identical to IBM's NetView/6000
 product except for the following, which are unavailable due to
 operating system differences:

 o  Host Connection/Service Point Functionality is not present

 o  The system monitoring sub-agent (trapgend) is not available for DEC
    OSF/1 AXP.

 POLYCENTER Manager on NetView and NetView/6000 are based on HP's
 OpenView, the same code used in OSF's DME Network Management Option
 which is now under development at the OSF (Open Software Foundation).

 INSTALLATION

 POLYCENTER Manager on NetView by itself is customer installable,
 however it does require proper configuration of underlying UNIX
 services, particularly the TCP/IP network services. Digital
 Installation Services are available for this product.

 Customer Responsibilities

 Before installation of the above software, the customer must:

 o  Previously have installed and configured all requisite software.

 o  Registered and activated the License PAK on the designated system.

 HARDWARE REQUIREMENTS

 o  A suitable Alpha AXP processor listed below
 o  At least 64 MB of RAM (96 MB suggested)
 o  A color display with 1280 x 1024 resolution

 Processors Supported

 Alpha AXP:
 DEC 2000 Model 300 AXP Workstation
 DEC 2000 Model 500 AXP Workstation
 DEC 3000 Model 300 AXP Workstation
 DEC 3000 Model 300 AXP Server
 DEC 3000 Model 300L AXP Workstation
 DEC 3000 Model 300L AXP Server
 DEC 3000 Model 400 AXP Workstation
 DEC 3000 Model 400 AXP Server
 DEC 3000 Model 500 AXP Workstation
 DEC 3000 Model 500 AXP Server
 DEC 3000 Model 500X AXP Workstation
 DEC 3000 Model 500X AXP Server
 DEC 3000 Model 600 AXP Server
 DEC 3000 Model 600 AXP Workstation
 DEC 3000 Model 800 AXP Workstation
 DEC 3000 Model 800 AXP Server
 DEC 4000 Model 610 AXP System
 DEC 4000 Model 710 AXP System
 DEC 7000 Model 610 AXP System
 DEC 10000 Model 610 AXP System

 Processors Not Supported:

 This product does not support VAX-based or RISC-based processors.

 Disk Space Requirements:

 /usr/OV =                  200,000 Kbytes

  swap space =               150,000 Kbytes

 More swap space will be needed for larger networks, or when other
 memory-intensive products run on the same system.

 Additional space will be required for databases and log files.

 GROWTH CONSIDERATIONS

 The minimum hardware/software requirements for any future version of
 this product may be different from the requirements for the current
 version. Additional memory and/or disk space may be required to monitor
 large networks.

