 ................   T H E M E   O F   T H E   M O N T H ...............

                   NETWORKING AND NETWORK MANAGEMENT

 NETWORKS FOR THE CAMPUS........Many of Digital's customers are facing
 increasing demands on their networks today, as they plan and implement
 bandwidth-demanding applications in areas such as imaging and multi-
 media. At the same time, the increase in downsized applications and the
 move to client/server computing are placing increased performance and
 response time demands on network investments already made. Institutions
 need to incorporate new networking technologies as they tie independent
 administrative and academic LANs into an integrated campus-wide LAN
 capable of handling high bandwidth and gateways to other academic and
 commercial partners. At the same time, institutions want to ensure that
 there is no negative impact on network availability while they upgrade,
 and they want to extend the useful life of their previous network
 investments as far as practical. Digital provides leading-edge techno-
 logy solutions that preserve previous investments, and provide the
 network management tools to ensure that customers also get the best
 performance and reliability from their networks.

 CAMPUS-WIDE NETWORK MANAGEMENT......Digital offers a suite of software
 tools to help customers manage and monitor their client/server environ-
 ments. Key networking and network management tools include POLYCENTER
 Manager on NetView, POLYCENTER DECnet Manager on NetView, ManageWORKS,
 HUBwatch, and PROBEwatch. These tools benefit Education and research
 institutions through lowered network support costs, increased network
 availability, and increased productivity.

   POLYCENTER MANAGER ON NETVIEW: POLYCENTER Manager on NetView for DEC
   OSF/1 AXP provides a comprehensive network management solution for
   heterogeneous multi-vendor network devices and open client/server
   networked environments. It includes user-oriented SNMP applications,
   providing network management functionality in the critical areas of
   fault, configuration, and performance management.

   POLYCENTER DECNET MANAGER ON NETVIEW: This is an application layered
   on top of POLYCENTER Manager on NetView designed to support the
   management of the DECnet environment in addition to IP management.
   The product gives users the ability to manage their Digital network
   environment including: DECnet Phase IV, DECnet/OSI, Terminal Servers,
   LAN Bridges, and FDDI.

   ManageWORKS: Part of Digital's PATHWORKS for DOS/Windows V5.0, this
   tool manages the client/server relationships in Novell NETware,
   Digital PATHWORKS, and Microsoft LAN Manager network operating system
   environments.

   HUBwatch: Manages the physical connectivity provided by Digital's
   DEChub family of products, reducing network downtime and support
   costs. It offers point-and-click LAN re-configuration for the DEChub
   900 Multiswitch, port statistics and security information for the
   DECrepeater 900TM, and management of the DECserver 900TM terminal
   server.

   PROBEwatch: Monitors LAN traffic and provides diagnostic and perfor-
   mance optimization recommendations. It also supports emerging
   standards for remote network traffic monitoring. PROBEwatch can
   identify host by MAC, IP, or DECnet address; identify vendor name
   based on MAC address decoding, decode many major network protocols,
   and perform off-line filter editing, storage, and retrieval.

