 ENHANCEMENTS TO GIGAswitch........GIGAswitch, Digital's FDDI switch, is
 a flexible, cost-effective way to create high-performance LANs, using
 existing FDDI technology. It provides investment protection for shared
 channel technologies by integrating them into switched-based FDDI
 networks. Recent enhancements to the GIGAswitch include: ATM linecard,
 48V DC power option, 4-port FDDI linecard, Unshielded Twisted Pair
 (UTP) Physical Media Device (PMD) support.

 * Fact Sheet - GIGAswitch Enhancements - news0606.txt

 * Public directory, SCHOOL::SONOMA_RM:[SONOMA_FW_RM.RELEASE], with
   technical details and the GIGAswitch V2.X System Release Notes. FTP
   to gatekeeper.dec.com with "anonymous" as the login and your email
   address as the password. The internet address for the gatekeeper
   is 16.1.0.2.

 INTERNET SECURITY SERVICES......Network security should be an integral
 part of any institution's network management strategy. Digital recently
 announced its Internet Security Services, which combines consulting and
 software to deliver a protected and programmable "firewall" that guards
 access to the institution's networks while giving users access to the
 Internet and other external networks. The announcement of Internet
 Security Services was also featured in the May issue of DECNEWS.

 * Fact Sheet - Internet Security Services; news0607.txt

 ..................... A N N O U N C E M E N T S ......................

 DIGITAL LAUNCHES "INTERNET-READY" SYSTEM WITH COMMERCIAL MOSAIC......
 Digital will soon begin providing the Mosaic navigation tool for the
 Internet with its computer systems, under a licensing agreement with
 Spyglass, Inc. of Champaign, Illinois. Mosaic, a global "browser",
 allows users to search for and retrieve, display, store, and forward
 documents and data from anywhere in the world via the Internet. It
 works in conjunction with the Internet's World Wide Web, a diverse
 collection of information servers. Spyglass is a commercial licensee of
 Mosaic for the National Center for Supercomputing Applications (NCSA)
 at the University of Illinois/Urbana-Champaign, developer of Mosaic.
 Digital plans to offer Mosaic on all of its computer systems, including
 its Alpha AXP and Intel personal systems and others running the DEC
 OSF/1, OpenVMS, Windows, and Windows NT operating systems and the
 PATHWORKS network operating system. Mosaic supports Digital's S.E.A.L.
 and Internet Security Services. The agreement with Spyglass also allows
 for the Mosaic license to be included under the Campuswide Software
 License Grant (CSLG) and DECcampus programs.

 For more information, send an e-mail message to: info@digital.com or
 access our Web Server at http://web.digital.com/home.html

 UNIVERSITIES AT THE HELM OF NEW AXP SYSTEMS ON THE INTERNET......Two
 new DEC 3000 Model 800 AXP workstations have recently been added to the
 internet, expanding Digital's Alpha AXP Internet Program to four
 systems. Stanford University in California, and the University of
 Texas, Austin will manage the internet connection of these AXP systems
 for one year. To test OSF/1 and OpenVMS AXP on the DEC 3000, telnet or
 rlogin as indicated below. Login as username axpguest (no password
 required) to register for an account.

   *  OSF/1: axposf.stanford.edu
   *  OpenVMS: axpvms.cc.utexas.edu

 DIGITAL AND TOUCH TECHNOLOGIES ANNOUNCE JOINT PRODUCT PARTNERSHIP....
 Digital and Touch Technologies, Inc. have announced a partnership
 through which Touch will assume full responsibility for the development
 and maintenance of several Digital software applications. Included in
 the partnership are the VAX DOCUMENT, DECquery, DECcalc, DECdecision,
 DECgraph, and DECslide software products. Under the agreement, Digital
 will act as a Touch Technologies distributor, selling and distributing
 the products under the current names and order numbers, and continuing
 as the service provider. The partnership was designed to ensure
 security and continuity for Digital customers. Touch Technologies plans
 to move forward with upgrades to existing product features, as well as
 address the need for support on Alpha AXP. Digital has negotiated a
 special arrangement with Touch Technologies allowing the products to
 remain in both the Campuswide Software License Grant (CSLG) and
 DECcampus Programs.

 NEW ALPHA AXP WORKSTATION PORTS FOR COMPUTATIONAL CHEMISTRY..Hypercube,
 Inc. of Ontario, Canada recently announced the availablity of four
 computational chemistry codes on OSF/1 AXP. HyperMM+ and HyperNewton
 are their new molecular mechanics software, and HyperEHT and HyperNDO
 their new semi-empirical molecular orbital software. These codes are
 designed to take advantage of the computational power of an Alpha AXP
 workstation server. Hyperchem, Hypercube's very popular Hyperchem PC
 software, can "farm out" computationally intensive tasks to these
 programs on an OSF/1 Alpha AXP server on the network.

 * Contact: Hypercube, Inc., 419 Philips St, Unit 7, Waterloo Ontario
   N2L3X2, Canada Phone: 519-725-4040

 PVM SOFTWARE NOW AVAILABLE ON OPENVMS........PVM (Parallel Virtual
 Machine), the popular library for linking workstations into farms or
 clusters for parallel computing applications, is now available for the
 OpenVMS operating system. Up until now, it has been available for
 Digital systems running OSF/1 or Ultrix. The OpenVMS version of PVM is
 available via ftp from: The Oregon Graduate Institute (ftp cse.ogi.edu)
 in the directory pub/otto/PVM_VMS. This software is initially intended
 for VAX systems but will be qualified on Alpha OpenVMS systems shortly.

 Questions on the software will be answered by: Dan L. Clark, Oregon
 Graduate Institute, dclark@cse.ogi.edu, (503) 230-4400.

 NEW STORAGEWORKS SUBSYSTEMS EXPAND SCSI CONNECTIVITY........Digital
 recently announced a new StorageWorks subsystem controller that
 increases locally attached SCSI disk connectivity and extends I/O
 performance. The HSZ40 StorageWorks Array Controller allows up to 42
 industry-standard SCSI-2 disk devices to be connected to a single SCSI
 port, expanding local disk storage to support applications and user
 growth. The new controller is supported on Digital OSF/1 AXP V2.0, with
 OpenVMS AXP support planned for the near future. This capability
 addresses the demands for scalable storage solutions supported across
 multiple platforms using industry-standards and common interconnects.

 For more information in the U.S. call 1-800-STORWORK.

 * Info Sheet - HSZ40 StorageWorks Array Controller; news0608.txt

 DIGITAL'S UNIX SYSTEM BREAKS FILE SERVICE PERFORMANCE BARRIER.....
 Digital's AdvantageCluster Fileserver 3000 system provides over 51%
 greater throughput than Network Appliance's FAstserver, and more than
 69% shorter response time than the SPARCcluster Model 4 from Sun
 Microsystems, thus exceeding the performance and response time of the
 highest performing systems from any other vendor. This performance
 breakthrough results from Digital's most recent testing using the SFS
 benchmark developed and administered by the System Performance Evalua-
 tion Committee (SPEC). The SFS benchmark test determines throughput and
 response times for file services in UNIX networks. The AdvantageCluster
 Fileserver is a member of Digital's expanding AdvantageCluster product
 family of UNIX clusters, which provide industry-leading scalability and
 availability solutions.

 * Press Release and Benchmark Results - news0609.txt;

