 news0604.txt; - Digital HUBwatch Information Sheet

 HUBwatch

 Easy-to-Use SNMP Graphical Network Management for the DEChub Family

 Chances are, you invested in Digital's modular DEChub family to gain
 control over your network wiring. But powerful features alone aren't
 enough. You need ease of use because your time is valuable and
 flexibility because your network is always changing. Digital designed
 HUBwatch to meet these critical needs. HUBwatch features a friendly
 graphical interface and SNMP (Simple Network Management Protocol),
 which lets you manage your networks remotely -- from anywhere on the
 network.

 HUBwatch gives you instant access to the DEChub's full power -- simply
 by clicking on a mouse. In fact, HUBwatch is so easy to use you
 probably won't even have to refer to a manual. Have a question? Just
 click on the award-winning online help capabilities of HUBwatch for
 extensive, context-sensitive help.

 Since HUBwatch translates SNMP messages into pictures, you can easily
 manage any DEChub -- from an individual stackable module to a DEChub
 900 MultiSwitch -- right from your desk. For example, you can balance
 network traffic and allocate bandwidth by switching modules in the
 DEChub 900 to different LAN channels. And you can do this with software
 via a mouse -- instead of finding the hub, turning it off, and
 physically moving connections.

 HUBwatch helps you save time, reduce management expenses, and create a
 more efficient network. By controlling all the hub functions, HUBwatch
 reduces your network downtime and decreases network support costs --
 because even a non-technical person can manage DEChubs using the simple
 graphical interface. Additionally, HUBwatch reduces the cost and
 inconvenience of change since traffic can be switched to a different
 LAN via software, rather than manually.

 Highlights

 o  Offers simple point-and-click commands, descriptive icons, and
    context-sensitive help for easy management

 o  Uses the same software and a consistent user interface to manage the
    entire DEChub Family -- from stackable modules to the DEChub 900

 o  Lets you reconfigure LANs via a mouse

 o  Provides full repeater management with statistics and security down
    to the port level

 o  Provides an identical graphical user interface for both in-band and
    out-of-band access

 o  Is available on MS(r) Windows(tm) and OpenVMS VAX

 o  The OpenVMS VAX version can be launched from the POLYCENTER network
    map

 Manages Remotely from Anywhere on the Network

 Digital's HUBwatch management solution gives you the flexibility to
 manage modules anywhere on the network, in or out of the hub -- right
 from your desk. And since each DEChub 900 module contains its own SNMP
 agent, you don't have togive up a slot for a management card.

 Grows with Your Network

 Whether you need to manage a small PC LAN or an extensive enterprise-
 wide network, Digital's HUBwatch software provides the management your
 network needs. As your network grows larger and more complex, it's easy
 to add more management functions. You can layer HUBwatch on Digital's
 enterprise management tools to integrate management of other Digital
 and multivendor networking devices, or you can manage your local
 DEChub-based LAN using your PC and HUBwatch for Windows.

 Reconfiguring Your LAN

 HUBwatch is built on technology that exceeds expectations. Not only is
 it powerful, but it's also simple to use. For example, to connect a
 module to a different LAN, just click on the connection box at the end
 of the green line and drag it to a new LAN. That's all there is to it!
 HUBwatch will not allow you to make an incorrect connection. And it's
 just as simple to create new LANs and choose which technology they will
 use. You need only the keyboard to enter the name of the LAN.

 Managing Repeaters

 Identifying and diagnosing repeater problems is easy with HUBwatch.
 Suppose you are notified of a problem on a particular hub. Simply point
 and click on the appropriate hub to bring up its picture. If you don't
 already know which repeater port is having problems, the LEDs on the
 hub view screen will identify the faulty port. Or you can click on a
 repeater to get a summary screen and examine traffic gauges. If you
 want more information about a specific port, just click on that port --
 either on the hub view or the repeater summary view -- to view the port
 information screen. This redundant point-and-click capability lets you
 navigate through the software quickly using as much, or as little,
 information as you need to manage the hub.

 You can enable or disable repeater ports from either the summary or
 detail screens. HUBwatch also supplies you with all the statistical
 information that you need -- octets, frames, collisions, and errors --
 with easy-to-read gauges. If you want more statistics, the details
 button will give you access to 14 different counters. In addition,
 using active icons and simple screen layouts, HUBwatch lets less
 experienced users manage the hub, while still providing the data
 necessary to do the job.

 Ensuring Network Security

 Security is always a consideration when choosing a network management
 solution. HUBwatch provides full security to the port level --
 preventing network intrusion and eavesdropping.

 Managing Other DEChub ONE Devices on the Network

 In addition to managing the DEChub 90 and DEChub 900MS, HUBwatch lets
 you manage standalone DEChub ONE products. Simply double-click on the
 picture of the individual module and you bring up the same detailed
 screens whether the module is standalone or in a hub.

 Future Directions

 HUBwatch is continually being improved to handle new modules,
 additional platforms, and additional Digital network devices. Version
 3.0 for OpenVMS VAX will add support for the FDDI DECconcentrator
 900MX, the multi-port Ethernet-to-FDDI bridge, DECbridge 900MX, all the
 new Ethernet DECrepeaters (90FS, 900FP, and 900GM), and GIGAswitch.
 HUBwatch for OpenVMS VAX 3.0 has also been enhanced to send an alarm
 when a user-defined threshold has been exceeded. More Digital and
 non-Digital platforms will be added in the future. HUBwatch is designed
 to provide you with an easy-to-use network manager that runs on a
 platform you already use and consistently manages all of Digital's
 network hardware.

 For More Information

 For more information about HUBwatch or any other Digital product or
 service, please contact your local Digital sales office or authorized
 Digital reseller.

 Hardware Prerequisites

 o  For HUBwatch for Windows V.2.0: 80386DX 33 MHz or faster PC, 8 MB
    RAM, 20 MB hard disk space

 o  For HUBwatch for OpenVMS VAX V.3.0: See SSA 40.64 for DECstation and
    DECsystem configurations

 o  DECagent 90 on the same LAN to manage DECbridge 90s and DECserver 90
    L/L+ and in the DEChub 90 to manage the DECrepeater 90s (DECagent
    not required to manage DECrepeater 90s in DEChub 900)

 Software Prerequisites

 For Windows

 o  MS-DOS 5.0 or higher
 o  Windows 3.1
 o  NDIS driver for the PCs Ethernet NIC card

 For OpenVMS VAX

 o  OpenVMS VAX 5.4 or 5.5
 o  DECwindows Motif
 o  TCP/IP Services for OpenVMS VAX (included with NAS 250 services) or
    TGV Multinet

 Digital believes the information in this publication is accurate as of
 its publication date; such information is subject to change without
