 news0606.txt; GIGAswitch Enhancements - Fact Sheet

 DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION FACT SHEET

 PRODUCT NAME:  GIGAswitch Enhancements

 OVERVIEW:

 GIGAswitch, Digital's FDDI switch, is a flexible, cost-effective way to
 create high-performance LANs, using existing FDDI technology.
 GIGAswitch provides investment protection for shared channel
 technologies by integrating them into switched-based FDDI networks.
 New options for GIGAswitch are:

 o  ATM linecard, providing GIGAswitch-to-GIGAswitch connectivity via
    ATM links, conventional clear channel T3, or clear channel
    point-to-point circuits. The FDDI network can be expanded with the
    confidence that investment in GIGAswitch will be protected as the
    migration to ATM technology progresses.

 o  48V DC power option, enabling the GIGAswitch system to directly
    connect to DC power sources common to telephone switching
    environments (e.g. "Central Office").

 o  4-port FDDI linecard, increasing system capacity to 34 FDDI
    connections.

 o  Unshielded Twisted Pair (UTP) Physical Media Device (PMD) support,
    enabling GIGAswitch connections via category 5 UTP copper cabling.

 o  New firmware V2, adding new features and capabilities to GIGAswitch.

 KEY FEATURES:

 o  The ATM linecard is a 2-port linecard that interfaces to T3, OC-3,
    or ATM, facilitating wide area connections between GIGAswitches at
    either 155 Mb/s SONET/SDH or 45 Mb/s DS3. Provides seamless
    migration from switched FDDI LANs to high-speed WANs such as ATM.

 o  Optional 48V DC provides alternative for withstanding AC power
    outages.

 o  The 4-port FDDI linecard provides four single attachment station
    (SAS) connections. It increases the number of FDDI network
    connections (for example, high-performance servers, workstations,
    other GIGAswitches) to 34, enabling additional point-to-point
    connections and/or integration of more FDDI LANs to form a
    gigabit-class switched backbone network.

 o  Support for multiple media types (multimode and single mode fiber,
    and UTP) gives customers options relative to their distance and
    applications requirements, and use of the existing cable
    infrastructure.

 o  A key enhancement included in Version 2 firmware, an Address
    Resolution Protocol (ARP) server is integral to the GIGAswitch and
    efficiently provides IP address mapping to requesting stations.

 PRICING AND AVAILABILITY: (NOTE: U.S. ONLY)

 The GIGAswitch ATM linecard begins at $18,000 with availability in
 June 1994.

 The 48V DC power supply is $3K with availability in June 1994.

 The 4-port FDDI UTP linecard is $13.5K with availability in June
 1994.

 Version 2 firmware is included with all GIGAswitches at no
 additional cost, beginning in May 1994.



