SUMMARY

Based on current performance and future trends, the Alpha AXP
family of processors and platforms will provide superb servers
for high-end production systems. To keep pace with the phenomenal
increases in CPU speed, database systems must incorporate
features that reduce the I/O bottleneck. DEC Rdb version 6.0
software has incorporated a number of these features:
asynchronous page fetch, asynchronous batch write, multithreaded
backup and restore, multi-statement procedures, and AIJ log
server using electronic caches. These enhancements not only allow
optimal transaction processing performance but also permit
systems to deal with very large data sets.

