PC Message Server Program Announcement

HIGHLIGHTS

o  PC Message Server hardware/software product will integrate with E-mail,
   telephone, and FAX systems to offer message access and management
   anywhere, anytime

o  Will operate on Alpha AXP EISA bus systems running Windows NT and NT
   Advanced Server software

o  Initial release available this summer

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The PC Message Server, an integrated hardware/software product based on
Digital and third-party technology, will let users access their E-mail
accounts and manage their mail messages via standard or cellular telephone.

Users will be able to have mail messages read to them over the telephone,
save, forward, or delete messages, or FAX messages to remote locations.
Administrative tools will allow the PC Message Server to manage subscribers
remotely, and access codes will provide user specific security.

The PC Message Server will run on scalable, high performance Alpha AXP
systems under the Windows NT and NT Advanced Server operating systems.

BENEFITS

The PC Message Server will help increase customer responsiveness and
employee productivity, contributing to a cost-effective, dependable
departmental computing environment.

