DECtalk Express Speech Synthesizer

HIGHLIGHTS

o  High quality DECtalk text-to-speech synthesis technology available in
   external product complementary to internal DECtalk PC Speech Synthesizer
   and compatible with latest (V4.2) DECtalk technology

o  Small, lightweight (15 ounces), and easily portable, with carrying case
   and detachable accessory pouch to facilitate transportation

o  Serial port allows for use with personal computer (IBM or compatible),
   laptop, notebook, palmtop, workstation, and Macintosh or other Apple
   system

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Many companies and individuals require the conversion of ASCII text into
speech output to facilitate fast and easy access to computer based
information. Furthermore, international standards and recent legislation
such as the Americans with Disabilities Act are now emphasizing workplace
accommodations for people with disabilities. However, the various
synthesized speech options available either offer output that is neither
natural sounding nor highly intelligible or do not address such user needs
as portability or platforms beyond IBM compatible PCs.

The DECtalk Express Speech Synthesizer (SPD 36.08.04) makes the leading
DECtalk speech synthesis technology available in a form that addresses the
need for a portable product that is compatible with a range of computing
platforms.

When used in conjunction with "screen access" or other business specific
applications, the DECtalk Express Speech Synthesizer allows users to hear
database and monitor-screen contents, messages, and other data through the
conversion of ASCII text into high quality speech output. Users who are
blind or have low vision and users with learning disabilities can have
computing access with this product and be more productive in the workplace
and at home. Employers can provide workplace accommodations for employees
and customers with disabilities.

Additional features and benefits include:

o  A speaking rate range of 75 to 650 words per minute for flexibility of
   use.
o  Patented automatic name pronunciation capabilities for greater
   naturalness.
o  Word-by-word indexing for a direct match between screen viewing and
   speech output.
o  Selectable volume level and headphones included for personal listening.

For further information please consult the following articles:

o  "DECtalk PC Speech Synthesizer Option," in the January 10, 1992, issue of
   Digital's Customer Update.
o  "DECtalk PC Speech Synthesizer V4.1," in the May 10, 1993, issue.
o  "DECtalk PC for DOS V4.2 Upgrade Kit," in the May 9, 1994, issue.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The DECtalk Express Speech Synthesizer is orderable now through the
DECdirect (800-344-4825) and DESKTOP DIRECT (800-722-9332) services, local
Digital sales offices, and Digital's business partners, for shipments
starting in July. Prepurchase technical assistance is available at
800-343-4040. A one-year return-to-factory warranty is included.

Order No.	 Description

