PATHWORKS V4.1 FOR OS/2 AND PATHWORKS V5.0 FOR OS/2

PATHWORKS V4.1 for OS/2 software (SPD 55.24.05) allows OS/2 workstations to
participate in DECnet Phase IV networks as end (nonrouting) nodes. OS/2
workstations can be connected to OpenVMS, DEC OSF/1, Windows NT, or OS/2
systems and can utilize selected resources and services of those systems.

PATHWORKS V4.1 for OS/2 software supports the latest releases of the OS/2
operating system plus the IBM LAN Server and Microsoft LAN Manager network
operating systems. PATHWORKS V4.1 for OS/2 layers on valid retail versions
of either network operating system, offering greater flexibility for OS/2
users.

The PATHWORKS V4.1 software provides DECnet support to OS/2 systems
configured as either clients or servers. Please note, however, that this
release is aimed primarily at integrating OS/2 servers into a PATHWORKS
environment; client applications are not included.

PATHWORKS V5.0 software will include a DECnet virtual device driver that
will permit DECnet based PATHWORKS for DOS/Windows applications to run on
OS/2 client systems.

Among the benefits of the new V4.1 release:

o  Users with Lotus Notes servers can now incorporate OS/2 Notes servers
   into PATHWORKS networks.

o  The V4.1 release has a simplified user installation procedure with a
   graphical user interface. The installation utility follows OS/2
   Presentation Manager paradigms, so users familiar with OS/2 will be
   comfortable using PATHWORKS V4.1 for OS/2.

PATHWORKS V4.1 for OS/2 software is available now through local Digital
sales offices and Digital's business partners. For explanations of PATHWORKS
licensing options, please refer to the "PATHWORKS Licensing Practices"
article in the October 25, 1993, issue of Digital's Customer Update.

