DECmodel FOR Windows V1.1

Companies that have engaged in business process reengineering as a means of
refocusing their work according to process rather than function require
powerful, intuitive methods and technologies to manage the implementation of
the changes required. DECmodel for Windows V1.1 is an easy-to-use tool that
helps users and consultants visualize and communicate the dynamics of
complex business processes. It addresses a variety of business
transformation services, including not only business process reengineering
but information technology consulting, organizational effectiveness, and
computer downsizing.

The DECmodel for Windows solution requires no programming background to
build and demonstrate models, and users from various industries can utilize
its powerful visualization capabilities. The enhancements in the V1.1
release include a simpler user interface and  advanced printing and model
development features. A summary of DECmodel for Windows features:

o  Builds working simulations of large business processes, generally in the
   form of user described architectures or high level designs of
   administrative systems

o  Works best on business and systems processes that are:
   - Cross-geographic.
   - Cross-organizational.
   - Critical to the operation of the business.
   - Not limited to one person or group possessing detailed knowledge of the
     entire system.

o  Uses standard enterprise modeling methodologies in conjunction with
   object-oriented simulation and modeling tools and techniques.

o  Provides a way to test, verify, and validate ideas for improving business
   operations before extensive investment.

o  Accelerates the discovery of efficient design while reducing costs
   associated with design changes.

o  Animates processes and shows how transactions represent business events
   -- with start and stop times, sequences, dependencies, initial
   conditions, behaviors, and changes in output.

o  The initial model can be modified to reflect actual changes or answer
   what-if questions.

o  Models can be modified to represent optimal operation, test alternatives,
   view the impact of parallel processes, and develop a roadmap for getting
   from the current system to the future vision.

o  Can instantly generate tabular reports of information stored within a
   model, which can then be exported to popular spreadsheet and word
   processing software.

o  Multiple-page printing lets users print larger paper representations of
   a model or simulation.

o  Toolbar added to accelerate most commonly used functions.

o  Attribute values can now be propagated through a sequence of activities.

DECmodel for Windows V1.1 offers the following benefits:

o  Communicates "why", "when," and "how" work gets done.
o  Technology is intuitive and easy to use.
o  Validates redesign before implementation.
o  Surfaces the conflicts needed to bring about process change.
o  Places power of discovery in the hands of change agents.
o  Provides rapid model building and prototyping.
o  Training and support are readily available.

