StorageWorks RAID Array 110 SUBSYSTEM FOR DEC OSF/1 V2.0

The StorageWorks RAID Array 110 subsystem is a complete, packaged hardware
based RAID subsystem that provides a way of configuring disk drives to
provide increased performance and/or data redundancy in the event of a drive
failure. It is now available for DEC 3000 Models 400, 500, 600, and 800
running DEC OSF/1 V2.0, in addition to its earlier availability on some
OpenVMS VAX systems and such Intel platforms as Sun systems and Novell
NetWare servers. It is supported by the KZTSA very high performance
TURBOchannel to SCSI adapter and the PMAZC TURBOchannel to SCSI adapter. It
supports RAID levels 0, 1, 0+1, and 5 and up to 30 disk drives.

For further information, including a complete product description plus
ordering and configuration data, please consult the "New Features for
StorageWorks RAID Array 110 Subsystem" article in the March 14, 1994, issue
of Digital's Customer Update (information is also available in the Systems
and Options Catalog).

The StorageWorks RAID Array 110 subsystem for DEC OSF/1 V2.0 systems is
available now through the DECdirect service, local Digital sales offices,
and Digital's business partners. Standard services are available. The
